{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1538645698,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzNjgxNTE5Nw=="},"target":"427c37a9fee0544d0bddae1f95e4ae735dad690d81f8e77c6549f89e371a78b9","message":"It is not documented that it needs to be a dict to not crash things.\n\nIt is unclear that it is redundant with `**kwargs`.\n\nI propose to remove `**kwargs`, in line with the `AnnexRepo` constructor. Moreover, I propose to rename `git_opts` to `git_init_opts` in both classes to make it clear that they are actually going to the `git init` call.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1538648554,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjk2NTQzMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2895#issuecomment-426965432"},"message":"The situation is more fucked up then expected. The flyweight pattern somehow expects to be able to pass any option to any repo class. For example `ok_clean_git` creates an instance of AnnexRepo, but the actual class the args end up in is a `GitRepo`.\n\n```\nAnnexRepo(path, init=False, create=False)\n```\n\nSo a `GitRepo` without `**kwargs` will not be able to work. Hence \"random\" stuff is routed to the git-init call. Only GyPythons option rendering prevents it from having an effect in this case, as `init=False` will cause no option to be added (more or less by accident).\n\nThis is a highly fragile construct.\n\nI will no go deeper into it, but instead work around it, as it seems like a possibly bottomless pit.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1541352658,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE5NDQ5MjM3NDg="},"added":["fixed-in-revolution"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1578820751,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50Mjk0MTExNTcxNg=="},"added":[],"removed":["fixed-in-revolution"]}]}